    {
      "body": "Closing as superseded by #47179 (draft, @bingxche), which covers this file — and does more:\n\n- it registers `test_fp8_fused_writer_hip.py` to `base-a-test-cpu` rather than my `stage-a-test-cpu-amd` (both are real suites today, but theirs is the CPU stage, which is where the file actually belongs since it mocks the aiter kernel), and\n- it fixes the reason this stayed silent: it extends `validate_all_suites()` so AMD registrations are checked too, while mine only repaired one file.\n\nTwo independent PRs touching the same five lines is worse than one, so I am standing down rather than asking anyone to choose between them. If #47179 does not land, this is a two-line change and I will happily reopen it.\n\nThanks to whoever would have reviewed it.",
